instruction:
This Java code passed basic linting. Are there deeper security issues?
```java
DocumentBuilderFactory f = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
Document doc = f.newDocumentBuilder().parse(input);
```

output:
Yes — linters typically miss xml external entity (xxe) (CWE-611). This is a high-severity issue.

Disable DTD and external entities to prevent XXE.

Fix:
```java
DocumentBuilderFactory f = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
f.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
f.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
Document doc = f.newDocumentBuilder().parse(input);
```

